{"abstract":[{"text":"The Fiedler vector: λ₂ and a unit eigenvector of it, with the canonical sign (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FiedlerVector"},{"text":"); nil when the graph is not connected.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fiedlerVector","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = false, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FiedlerVector","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"normalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s (34 n from 5,000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At least two vertices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at least 1."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" matrix–vector"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver answers and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached the default limits in the measurements."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L195","fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE13fiedlerVector10normalized9tolerance13maxIterationsAD07FiedlerF0VyxGSgSb_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"fiedlerVector(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fiedlerVector"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIde